{"title":"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> does <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56306de57a4524b820b8aceb4b444a225f793cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+x-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> factor into the product of two linear factors with integer coefficients?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f12379e8222904fb82a6992ff2791fe73c7a973f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1  \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 9 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"360\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56306de57a4524b820b8aceb4b444a225f793cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+x-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> to factor into a product of two linear factors, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d98c0dd5c440d071a8b31c8fa96d9d373a40d7ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+x-n = (x + a)(x + b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"217\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are integers.\n</p><p>By expansion of the product of the linear factors and comparison to the original quadratic,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39bfa39675e009796007f6b63059232acd222329.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = -n$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f781c7372a3a0aea2552c51259025e25826745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The only way for this to work if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer is if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2ef1a68274b26a0f25f7e645c164a1d67e70c846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = -b +1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Here are the possible pairs:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe526090ecb3eeace3ed0a09b9ffb791b04d9106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = -1, b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/2/f22f0954a431749b97bfc2194603561d9aaa80bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = -2, b = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69cdf7ec84ff918cbe7f21acf7543bf1bd243080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vdots$\" width=\"3\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d08483a3d6999d9f5470ddb7bdb478b04b6c6ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = -9, b = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>This gives us 9 integers for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bf9089f3c0ad5ee9fca030cfb06b487e559902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{D}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the quadratic formula, the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56306de57a4524b820b8aceb4b444a225f793cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+x-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/272de2378c61e0ec5e33b0fc3de2da0939180a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{4n+1}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"42\" />.  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56306de57a4524b820b8aceb4b444a225f793cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+x-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> to factor into two linear factors with integer coefficients, both roots must be integers and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd562ceaa0577b4a7f23a01f24b17de924542bd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> must be an odd perfect square.\n</p><p>All odd perfect squares have remainder <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd562ceaa0577b4a7f23a01f24b17de924542bd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> may be any odd perfect square between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf55a43e07220577be7b789ac66ea80a163aaeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cdot 1 + 1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb74fc64352fbe3afc550b1b1a556609a0d589d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 100 + 1 = 401$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd562ceaa0577b4a7f23a01f24b17de924542bd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> could be one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a3ef23927840433866feead61a0b526540dd3a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2, 5^2, ..., 17^2, 19^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d008d8882245f5f2bfca59a6cf940dd1e4c29fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56306de57a4524b820b8aceb4b444a225f793cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+x-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> factors into two linear factors with integer coefficients if and only if both its roots are integers.  Also, since the product of the roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee5df0d5b6736df591c2c12ce45cf2d71bba5e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-n$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" />, one root is positive while the other is negative.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the positive root.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735a02ac949f23506f25cd0b4950c7e707f1a66c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = a^2+a = a(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"21\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> may range from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, giving a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d008d8882245f5f2bfca59a6cf940dd1e4c29fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME\" title=\"1989 AHSME\">1989 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181316\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 294/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2490/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 148/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7851/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.512      1 -total\n 57.79%    7.230      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 39.77%    4.976      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10739:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017181316 and revision id 284438. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}